From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:40:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Report only reserved space as free to a 32-bit program
 on PS5.

A 32-bit program learns how much address space is free from
VirtualQuery. On i386, ntdll reports the space outside its reserved
areas as allocated, since the system keeps mappings there. Under WoW64
the 64-bit ntdll skipped that, so the range above 2 GiB looked free up
to 4 GiB even where the PS5 kernel already had mappings of its own and
the reservation could not take it (2042 of 2048 MiB).

Wanted: Weapons of Fate reserves the largest free block it finds for
its heap: it asked for 0x80000000 bytes, the allocation failed ("out of
memory for allocation"), and the game read through a null pointer.

On PS5 a WoW64 process now gets the i386 rule below 4 GiB: space
outside the reserved areas is reported as reserved, so the largest free
block is one the program can have.
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
index ca34415..d62fa53 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -6660,7 +6660,14 @@ static struct file_view *get_memory_region_size( char *base, char **region_start
             return view;
         }
     }
-#ifdef __i386__
+#if defined(__i386__) || defined(__PROSPERO__)
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    /* So too for a 32-bit program on PS5 below 4 GiB: the kernel keeps
+     * mappings of its own there, outside the reservations, and a program
+     * that reserves the largest free block it finds (Wanted: Weapons of
+     * Fate's heap) must only find room it can have. */
+    if (is_wow64() && (UINT_PTR)base < 0x100000000ull)
+#endif
     {
         struct reserved_area *area;
 
